sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/scaling-area-law> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Area law and wing loading under isometry (R2, R3) (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "In an isometric family an area scales as the square of the linear dimension and the weight per unit area (wing loading, stress) scales linearly with it." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean) from the physics thread's formal statements (physics/FORMAL-STATEMENTS.md, 2026-10-31; Galileo 1638 and Thompson 1917 ch. II for the idea); hypotheses named, no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "S ∝ L^2 ; W/S ∝ L" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **R2, area law.** -/
theorem areaLaw_ratio {S : ℝ → ℝ} {k : ℝ} (h : AreaLaw S k) {L₁ L₂ : ℝ} (h₁ : 0 < L₁) (h₂ : 0 < L₂) :
    S L₂ / S L₁ = (L₂ / L₁) ^ 2"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.AreaLaw" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.areaLaw_ratio", "Delphi.areaLaw_log", "Delphi.wingLoading_ratio", "Delphi.wingLoading_log" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Isometry of the area is a named hypothesis (AreaLaw); the theorem says nothing about any family being isometric." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Isometry of the area and of the mass (constant density): named hypotheses, measured to fail within one flying-fish species (Davenport 1992); Nothing about which family is isometric; the theorems bound only families that are. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/scaling-area-law> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/scaling-area-law> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-scaling-area-law> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-scaling-area-law> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.areaLaw_ratio with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 2 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean (320 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.areaLaw_ratio, Delphi.areaLaw_log, Delphi.wingLoading_ratio, Delphi.wingLoading_log: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 2 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [scaling-area-exponent-three] R2 mutant: area ratio claimed to be (L2/L1)^3. Rejected with 3 error(s): Scaling.lean:61:35: error: unsolved goals [scaling-wingloading-exponent-two] R3 mutant: wing loading claimed to scale as (L2/L1)^2. Rejected with 3 error(s): Scaling.lean:66:83: error: unsolved goals Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/scaling-area-law> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Isometry of the area and of the mass (constant density): named hypotheses, measured to fail within one flying-fish species (Davenport 1992); Nothing about which family is isometric; the theorems bound only families that are. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

